Date: Sat, 4 Apr 2026 11:20:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Store Log Entry URI for Redfish event
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Store Log Entry URI for a Redfish event. This is to ensure
the originating log entry can be tracked from the RF event.

This change modifies the event schema version from v1_4_0 to v1_7_0
only in one code path which involves filterAndSendEventLogs().
This code path is exclusively utilized to send EventLog entries
to subscribers.
These can be send in 2 ways
1. Filesystem inotify (/var/log filesystem)
2. D-Bus signal (phosphor-logging)

Both of the above options utilize the exact same code path:
sendEventsToSubs() → filterAndSendEventLogs() → formatEventLogEntry() →
sendEventToSubscriber()

So the changes done are limited to subscription events only
with no regression impact to other code paths or any other
functionality.

Client-facing changes:
 - Added LogEntry navigation property to event entries,
   linking back to the originating EventLog entry.
 - Addy MessageSeverity field to align with the
   DMTF Event schema.
 - Bumped Event schema version from v1_4_0 to v1_7_0, which
   is the minimum version that includes the LogEntry property.

Tested:
- Unit tests pass
- Built an image with my code, ran it in QEMU:
  1. Created a subscription pointing to my receiver service [1]
  2. Verified that the subscription has been created successfully [2]
  3. Injected a log entry with command: [3]. It injected a DBus
     log entry with a name that has a corresponding RF message ID.
  4. BMCWeb sent event to the receiver. See [4] it's a debug from the
     receiver web service which logged raw payload containing the
     newly added LogEntry and MessageSeverity fields along with the
     existing Severity field .
  5. Ran command to see the corresponding log entry from the
     LogService using the Log Entry ID from the RF event
     to ensure correct match: [5]
  6. Ran rf_service_validator against the QEMU instance.
- Verified against COMMON_ERRORS.md
- Verified newly added properties exist in both CSDL and Json schema
  https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/Event_v1.xml

